                <pb facs="0491" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.51/1358: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-07T19:00:00-03:00">November 7, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>529. Embassy’s telegram 522, November 6, 4 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d559-f1"/>
                    According to the Minister of Finance the following statement would be released
                    to the press this evening regarding Dr. Prebisch’s mission: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dr. Prebisch is going to the United States for the purpose of conversing
                            with officials of the Treasury Department, the Federal Reserve Bank and
                            other American Banks regarding various monetary and banking
                            matters.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
